-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Item proc spells for the Cataclysm high-end catalogue -- 417 spells
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 468 of the items in 05_cata_highend_import.sql carry an on-use or on-equip
-- spell. Following those through their triggered-spell chains gives 438 spells,
-- 21 of which already resolve in stock Spell.dbc; the other 417 are minted here.
--
-- APPLY THIS BEFORE 07_cata_highend_item_procs.sql. That file writes the
-- spellid_1..5 columns, and an item pointing at a spell that does not resolve
-- produces a boot warning.
--
-- Same source and column calibration as 01_cata_itemsets_phase1.sql: Cata 4.3.4
-- Spell.dbc + SpellEffect.dbc + SpellAuraOptions.dbc + SpellClassOptions.dbc read
-- through the wow-update-enUS-15211/15354/15595 StormLib patch chain. Effect
-- values carry DieSides = 1 with BasePoints = (cata value - 1), reproducing the
-- Cata amount under 3.3.5 rules.
--
-- Spell family masks were re-derived, never copied: 47 resolved to an exact 3.3.5
-- mask, 105 legitimately carry none (no mask in the source, or SpellFamilyName 0,
-- where 3.3.5 SpellInfo::IsAffected can never match and the mask is inert).
-- None were unresolvable.
--
-- KNOWN LIMITATION -- 28 of these spells carry a DUMMY, SCRIPT_EFFECT or
-- out-of-range effect, which is inert without C++. Their rows are minted anyway so
-- the item resolves, the tooltip renders and nothing warns at boot, but the effect
-- itself will not fire until a script is written. They are listed at the bottom.
--
-- spell_dbc is an ADDITIVE overlay -- this adds rows without restating stock ones.
-- Server-side only: the client shows no icon or tooltip until Spell.dbc is rebuilt
-- and deployed. Idempotent.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

